From 367232705c052ad09c94086fafbffcf5ceee8db1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 13:16:27 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 07/18] ROCm: gfx12 WMMA multi-row GEMV up to 16 rows

A batched speculative verify (bsz 2 x 8 rows) is 16 rows per linear, past the
multi-row GEMV's 8-row limit, so every linear in the verify and in the
DFlash2 draft forward fell to the cooperative tile GEMM. The WMMA kernel
already computes 16 rows: lane L loads A row L & 15, and the accumulator
holds rows 8 (L >> 4) + i, so lanes 16-31 carry rows 8-15. This reduces both
lane halves into the row-wise fused epilogue.

Ported from wt-tree e604fcc (GPU-validated there: rows 9-16 match
reconstruct + hgemm; lm_head at 16 rows 1.85 ms vs 7.5 ms). The gating part
of 409ee42 is already in rdna4-dev as exl3_gemv_wmma_enabled(device) with a
per-call env read and a per-device arch check, so the row guards just pass
the device.

- EXL3_GEMV_MAX_M defaults to 16 (clamp 1..16); 8 restores the old limit.
- Rows 9-16 need the WMMA path (integer bitrate, gfx12, EXL3_GEMV_WMMA=1);
  otherwise both entry points decline and the cooperative GEMM runs as
  before. The fdot2 kernels never see more than 8 rows.
- The multi-matrix form takes rows 9-16 only unweighted and single-token.
- The 8-row specialization keeps its scratch size and accumulator count.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
